bda url, vid, note=None, **kw: ...` - instance attribute shadows class method, no self passed. That's simpler and avoids polluting the class. But monkeypatch fixture is cleaner for cleanup. Since we create a fresh instance per test, instance attribute assignment doesn't pollute other tests. But the instructions say to use monkeypatch or pytest-mock if appropriate. I'll use monkeypatch on the class, or just assign on the instance. Assigning on the instance is fine since the instance is discarded. But to be safe and explicit, I'll use monkeypatch.setattr(ie, '_download_json', ...) - monkeypatch works on instances too and will restore after test (though instance is discarded anyway).\n\nSimilarly for `_extract_f4m_formats` and `_extract_m3u8_formats` - monkeypatch to return canned lists and record calls.\n\nNow the URLs. TVPlayIE._VALID_URL - let me recall from youtube-dl source:\n\n```python\n_VALID_URL = r'''(?x)\n    https?://\n        (?:www\\.)?\n        (?P<host>\n            (?:tvplay\\.lv|\n               tvplay\\.skaties\\.lv|\n               latvijasradio\\.lr1\\.lv|\n               ...\n            )/\n        )...\n```\n\nActually the real TVPlayIE _VALID_URL (from youtube-dl):\n\n```python\nclass TVPlayIE(InfoExtractor):\n    IE_DESC = 'MTG services'\n    _VALID_URL = r'''(?x)\n        (?:\n            mtgx:|\n            https?://\n                (?:www\\.)?\n                (?:\n                    tvplay\\.lv/(?:parraides|video)|\n                    ...\n                )\n                /\n            )\n        (?P<id>\\d+)\n    '''\n```\n\nI don't remember exactly. Let me check with get_info. The important thing: `_match_id(url)` must return the video id. I'll pick a URL that matches the real _VALID_URL. Let me get TVPlayIE info first.\n\nActually, since the extracted code is what matters, maybe the test should define its own minimal class? No - the extracted code defines `class TVPlayIE(InfoExtractor)` with only `_real_extract`. If the coverage target is this extracted file, then the test must import that file. But I don't know its filename. Hmm.\n\nGiven the ambiguity, the most robust approach: import from `youtube_dl.extractor.tvplay` (the real module), since the code is stated to be extracted from there and lines 237-334 correspond to the real file's `_real_extract`. The real TVPlayIE has more methods (like `_real_extract` plus maybe others), but `_real_extract` is the same code.\n\nWait, but actually in the real youtube-dl tvplay.py, `_real_extract` is much longer (handles viafree etc.)? Let me check. The real TVPlayIE in youtube-dl master:\n\n```python\nclass TVPlayIE(InfoExtractor):\n    IE_DESC = 'MTG services'\n    _VALID_URL = r'''(?x)\n        (?:\n            mtgx:|\n            https?://\n                (?:www\\.)?\n                (?:\n                    tvplay\\.lv/...\n```\n\nAnd `_real_extract`:\n\n```python\ndef _real_extract(self, url):\n    video_id = self._match_id(url)\n    geo_country = self._search_regex(\n        r'https?://[^/]+\\.([a-z]{2})', url,\n        'geo country', default=None)\n    if geo_country:\n        self._initialize_geo_bypass({'countries': [geo_country.upper()]})\n    video = self._download_json(\n        'http://playapi.mtgx.tv/v3/videos/%s' % video_id, video_id, 'Downloading video JSON')\n\n    title = video['title']\n\n    try:\n        streams = self._download_json(\n            'http://playapi.mtgx.tv/v3/videos/stream/%s' % video_id,\n            video_id, 'Downloading streams JSON')\n    except ExtractorError as e:\n        if isinstance(e.cause, compat_HTTPError) and e.cause.code == 403:\n            msg = self._parse_json(e.cause.read().decode('utf-8'), video_id)\n            raise ExtractorError(msg['msg'], expected=True)\n        raise\n    ...\n```\n\nYes, this matches the real youtube-dl TVPlayIE._real_extract. So lines 237-334 of youtube_dl/extractor/tvplay.py are this method. \n\nSo my tests should import `TVPlayIE` from `youtube_dl.extractor.tvplay`