youtube_dl.extractor.tvplay import TVPlayIE\n\n\nVIDEO_URL = 'http://www.tvplay.lv/parraides/3949851'  # adjust per _VALID_URL\nVIDEO_ID = '3949851'\n\n\nclass FakeDownloader(object):\n    params = {}\n\n    def add_progress_hook(self, ph):\n        pass\n\n    def to_screen(self, msg):\n        pass\n\n    def to_stderr(self, msg):\n        pass\n\n    def trouble(self, msg, tb=None):\n        pass\n\n    def report_warning(self, msg):\n        pass\n\n\ndef _video_json(**overrides):\n    video = {\n        'title': 'Test Title',\n        'description': 'Test description',\n        'format_title': 'Test Series',\n        'format_position': {'episode': 3, 'season': 2},\n        '_embedded': {'season': {'title': 'Season 2'}},\n        'duration': 120,\n        'created_at': '2015-01-02T03:04:05+00:00',\n        'views': {'total': 1234},\n        'age_limit': 16,\n        'sami_path': None,\n        'is_geo_blocked': False,\n    }\n    video.update(overrides)\n    return video\n\n\ndef _make_ie(monkeypatch, video_json, streams_json=None, streams_exc=None,\n             f4m_formats=None, m3u8_formats=None):\n    ie = TVPlayIE(FakeDownloader())\n\n    calls = {'f4m': [], 'm3u8': []}\n\n    def fake_download_json(url, video_id, note=None, *args, **kwargs):\n        assert video_id == VIDEO_ID\n        if '/videos/stream/' in url:\n            if streams_exc is not None:\n                raise streams_exc\n            return streams_json if streams_json is not None else {}\n        return video_json\n\n    def fake_extract_f4m_formats(f4m_url, video_id, f4m_id=None, fatal=True, **kwargs):\n        calls['f4m'].append(f4m_url)\n        return list(f4m_formats or [])\n\n    def fake_extract_m3u8_formats(m3u8_url, video_id, ext=None, *args, **kwargs):\n        calls['m3u8'].append(m3u8_url)\n        return list(m3u8_formats or [])\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(ie, '_download_json', fake_download_json)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(ie, '_extract_f4m_formats', fake_extract_f4m_formats)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(ie, '_extract_m3u8_formats', fake_extract_m3u8_formats)\n    ie._calls = calls\n    return ie\n```\n\nWait - monkeypatch.setattr on an instance: `monkeypatch.setattr(ie, '_download_json', fake_download_json)` sets instance attribute; when the test finishes, monkeypatch deletes it. Since it's an instance attribute, `self._download_json(url, ...)` calls `fake_download_json(url, ...)` without self. Good.\n\nBut careful: `_download_json` signature in InfoExtractor is `_download_json(self, url_or_request, video_id, note=..., ...)`. When called as `self._download_json('http://...', video_id, 'Downloading video JSON')`, with instance attribute function, it's called as `fake_download_json('http://...', video_id, 'Downloading video JSON')`. Good.\n\nNow tests:\n\n**Test 1: full happy path**\n\n```python\ndef test_full_extract(monkeypatch):\n    video_json = _video_json(\n        sami_path='http://sami.example.com/v3/12345_en.xml')\n    streams_json = {\n        'streams': {\n            'hls': 'http://hls.example.com/stream.m3u8',\n            'medium': 'http://cdn.example.com/video.mp4',\n            'high': 'rtmp://fms.example.com/app/playpath1',\n            'f4m_stream': 'http://f4m.example.com/stream.f4m',\n            'not_a_url': 12345,  # url_or_none -> None -> continue\n            'bad_rtmp': 'rtmp://noapp',  # regex fails -> continue\n        }\n    }\n    f4m = [{'format_id': 'hds-f4m', 'url': 'http://f4m.example.com/manifest', 'ext': 'flv'}]\n    m3u8 = [{'format_id': 'hls-main', 'url': 'http://hls.example.com/index.m3u8', 'ext': 'mp4', 'protocol': 'm3u8_native'}]\n    ie = _make_ie(monkeypatch, video_json, streams_json,\n                  f4m_formats=f4m, m3u8_formats=m3u8)\n    result = ie._real_extract(VIDEO_URL)\n\n    assert result['id'] == VIDEO_ID\n    assert result['title'] == 'Test Title'\n    assert result['description'] == 'Test description'\n    assert result['series'] == 'Test Series'\n    assert result['episode_number'] == 3\n    assert result['season'] == 'Season 2'\n    assert result['season_number'] == 2\n    assert result['duration'] == 120\n    assert result['timestamp'] == parse_iso8601('2015-01-02T03:04:05+00:00')\n    assert result['view_count'] == 1234\n    assert result['age_limit'] == 16\n    assert result['subtitles'] == {'en': [{'url': 'http://sami.example.com/v3/12345_en.xml'}]}\n\n    formats = result['formats']\n    # f4m and m3u8 formats extended\n    assert f4m[0] in formats\n    assert m3u8[0] in formats\n    # plain http format\n    plain = [f for f in formats if f.get('format_id') == 'medium'][0]\n    assert plain['url'] == 'http://cdn.example.com/video.mp4'\n    assert plain['ext'] == 'mp4'\n    assert plain['quality'] == qualities(['hls', 'medium', 'high'])('medium')\n    # rtmp format\n    rtmp = [f for f in formats if f.get('format_id') == 'high'][0]\n    assert rtmp['ext'] == 'flv'\n    assert rtmp['url'] == 'rtmp://fms.example.com/app'\n    assert rtmp['app'] == 'app'\n    assert rtmp['play_path'] == 'playpath1'\n    assert rtmp['preference'] == -1\n    # f4m called with updated query\n    assert ie._calls['f4m'] == ['http://f4m.example.com/stream.f4m?hdcore=3.5.0&plugin=aasp-3.5.0.151.81']\n    assert ie._calls['m3u8'] == ['http://hls.example.com/stream.m3u8']\n```\n\nWait, `update_url_query` - the order of query params. `update_url_query(video_url, {'hdcore': '3.5.0', 'plugin': 'aasp-3.5.0.151.81'})` produces `...?hdcore=3.5.0&plugin=aasp-3.5.0.151.81`. In Python 3.7+, dict ordering is preserved, so hdcore first. OK.\n\nAlso note: `qualities(['hls', 'medium', 'high'])` returns a function mapping format_id to quality number. 'medium' -> 1, 'high' -> 2, 'hls' -> 0, unknown -> -1. Let me check `qualities`:\n\n```python\ndef qualities(quality_ids=()):\n    def q(qid):\n        try:\n            return quality_ids.index(qid)\n        except ValueError:\n            return -1\n    return q\n```\n\nYes. So 'medium' -> 1.\n\nFor the m3u8 branch: `_extract_m3u8_f