 That covers the branch where geo_country is falsy.\n\nAlternatively, use a URL with an IP or localhost... but it must match _VALID_URL. Let me check _VALID_URL first.\n\nActually, wait. Even simpler: the geo regex searches for `https?://[^/]+\\.([a-z]{2})` anywhere in the URL. If _VALID_URL allows e.g. `https://tvplay.skaties.lv/...` - that has `.lv` -> matches. Hmm.\n\nWhat about `mtgx:` scheme? In youtube-dl's TVPlayIE:\n\n```python\n_VALID_URL = r'''(?x)\n    (?:\n        mtgx:|\n        https?://\n            (?:www\\.)?\n            (?:\n                tvplay\\.lv/|\n                ...\n            )\n        )\n    (?P<id>\\d+)\n'''\n```\n\nI believe there's an `mtgx:` prefix option. Let me verify with get_info.\n\nIf not, I can use a URL like `http://www.tvplay.lv/parraides/3949851?x=1` - still matches geo regex. Hmm.\n\nWhat about a URL where the TLD part has uppercase or the domain ends without 2 lowercase letters? E.g., `https://www.tvplay.lv.evil.com/...`? That would match `co`... hmm `[^/]+\\.([a-z]{2})` on `www.tvplay.lv.evil.com` -> greedy: `[^/]+` = `www.tvplay.lv.evil`, `\\.` = `.`, `([a-z]{2})` = `co`. So geo_country = 'co'. Still matches.\n\nTo NOT match: the URL must have no `https?://` at all (e.g., `mtgx:12345`), or the part after `https?://` up to first `/` must not contain `.xx` pattern with 2 lowercase letters after a dot. E.g., `http://localhost/...` - but does _VALID_URL allow localhost? No.\n\nSo `mtgx:` scheme is the way, if supported. Let me check.\n\nActually, hold on. Even if geo_country is None, the branch `if geo_country:` is just skipped - that's a branch we need to cover (the false branch). Both branches need coverage for full branch coverage. Test 1 covers True branch; Test 6 covers False branch.\n\nIf `mtgx:` isn't supported by _VALID_URL, another option: monkeypatch `_match_id` to return the id and pass any URL string. Since `_real_extract` calls `self._match_id(url)`, I could monkeypatch `ie._match_id = lambda url: VIDEO_ID`